  "description": "Read-path client for the RagMeUp engine: exact vector ranking over a\n      candidate chunk-id set your own SQL produces (so RLS and filters stay\n      yours), passage building, cross-encoder reranking, and span reads for\n      grounded answers. Postgres + pgvector.",
  "id": "RagMeUp.Client",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-08-07T17:12:22.7Z",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "hRZMW5VaVimhaa9iEpVqdPZj9eXcqv6xrdKpMnBq3xgaBgVsVyIjwZi9BtxlN847Ce2BYq7M4nJ/FCEeZkxGpQ==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 75405,
  "published": "2026-08-07T17:09:45.103Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.3.0 — reranking granularity, engine-owned length guard, small-to-big reads.\n\n      BREAKING: Rerank(...) and ReadSpans(...) take a new optional parameter before\n      CancellationToken; pass ct as a named argument. Rerank now defaults to\n      ScoreGranularity.Chunk (scores each member chunk, folds with max) instead of\n      scoring the welded run — pass ScoreGranularity.Passage to keep 0.2.0\n      behaviour. ConfidenceDiagnosis gained NoDiscrimination.\n\n      * ScoreGranularity keeps the scored unit at chunk size, so a backend that\n        stops discriminating past ~1500 characters is no longer handed ~2250-char\n        welded runs. Folds with max, not sum, so a run ranks on its best part\n        rather than on its length.\n      * RerankCalibration.UsablePassageChars and RerankOutcome.Diagnostics carry\n        the engine's measured passage-length limit and what the run looked like,\n        replacing the constant consumers were hard-coding.\n      * ConfidenceDiagnosis.NoDiscrimination separates \"the reranker did not rank\"\n        from \"the corpus has no answer\" — previously a silent, total abstention.\n      * ChunkMatch/Passage carry HeadingPath and the enclosing section span;\n        ReadSpans(SpanWidth.Section) widens a precise hit to its section for\n        synthesis. Requires re-ingestion to populate; older rows fall back.",
